course: dictionary
lesson: 1969
title: Complain and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To complain is to say that you are not happy about something, or that something is wrong. «Next day Chloe's mum came in to complain that her daughter's head had been sore for days.» Mum came in to say that something was wrong, so complain means to tell someone about a problem.
explain: Look at the words after complain. They are clues. Complain about means you are not happy with something. Complain to means you tell someone in charge, so they can fix it. Complain of means you say you have a pain or illness. Swap in "say you are not happy" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Complaining can be helpful or annoying. A calm, polite complaint can get a broken toy changed at a shop. Complaining all the time can make you seem negative, so it helps to suggest a solution too. Read the rest of the text to see which kind of complaint it is.
fact: Complain is a verb: complain, complains, complained, complaining.
fact: «Complain about» means to say you are not happy with something.
fact: «Complain to» someone means telling a person in charge about a problem, so they can fix it.
fact: «Complain of» a pain or illness means to say that you have it.
fact: A complaint is the noun: you can make a complaint to a shop or a company when something goes wrong.
exercise: «Next day Chloe's mum came in to complain that her daughter's head had been sore for days.» What does complain mean here? | To sing a happy song in the shop | *To say that something is wrong and ask for it to be fixed | To forget something important | To buy a new hat for the day
exercise: Which phrase means to tell the person in charge about a problem so they can fix it? | complain of a sore arm | complain happily | complain about the rain | *complain to the shopkeeper
exercise: «He complained of a sore tooth all morning.» What does complained of mean here? | *Said that he had a sore tooth | Bit into a sweet | Lost his tooth | Gave his tooth a bath
test: Which word is the past tense of complain? | complain | complaining | complains | *complained
test: «Jamal said he had nothing to complain about after the trip.» What does this suggest? | He was lost on the way | He was hungry | *He was happy and satisfied with the trip | He was very cross
exam: «A self-checkout scanner complains when there is an unexpected item in the bagging area.» What does complains mean in this sentence? | *It signals that something is wrong | It switches itself off for ever | It weighs the bag twice | It sings a happy tune
